.SH "NAME"
gfarm-prun \- execute a command on multiple hosts
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.HP \w'\fBgfarm\-prun\fR\ 'u
\fBgfarm\-prun\fR [\fIoptions\fR] \fIcommand\fR [\fIarg\fR...]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
\fBgfarm\-prun\fR
executes
\fIcommand\fR
with
\fIarg\fRs on each host listed in a hostfile, by using a remote shell command,
\fBssh\fR
by default\&. It is useful, for example, to set up or manage filesystem nodes of Gfarm\&.
.PP
By default, the command is executed on one host after another\&. When the \-p option is specified, the command is executed on multiple hosts in parallel\&.
.PP
The hostfile has one host name in each line\&. Only the first field of each line is used\&. Characters from `#\*(Aq to the end of the line are regarded as a comment, and empty lines are ignored\&. The default hostfile is
$HOME/\&.nodelist\&.
.PP
The local host is skipped unless the \-a option is specified\&. A host is regarded as the local host when its name matches the output of
\fBhostname\fR
or one of the IP addresses displayed by
\fBhostname \-I\fR\&. These names can be changed by the PRUN_HOSTNAME environment variable\&.
.PP
The command line is passed to the remote shell command, thus it is interpreted by a shell on the remote host\&. Wildcards in the command line are expanded on the remote host, not on the local host\&.
.PP
Unless the \-stdin option is specified, the standard input of the remote command is
/dev/null\&.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.PP
\fB\-a\fR
.RS 4
Executes the command also on the local host, if it is listed in the hostfile\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-h\fR \fIhostfile\fR
.RS 4
Specifies a hostfile\&. If `\-\*(Aq is specified, the list of hosts is read from the standard input\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-m\fR \fImax_jobs\fR
.RS 4
Specifies the maximum number of hosts on which the command is executed in parallel with the \-p option\&. The default is 16\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-n\fR
.RS 4
Displays the commands that would be executed, but does not execute them\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-p\fR
.RS 4
Executes the command on multiple hosts in parallel in the background\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-rsh\fR \fIrsh_command\fR
.RS 4
Specifies a remote shell command\&. The default is
\fBssh\fR\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-stdin\fR \fIfile\fR
.RS 4
Specifies a file that is given to the standard input of the command on each host\&. This option can be specified multiple times\&. In this case, the files are concatenated\&. If `\-\*(Aq is specified, the standard input of
\fBgfarm\-prun\fR
is read once, and it is given to the command on each host\&. `\-\*(Aq cannot be specified for both the \-h option and the \-stdin option\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-v\fR
.RS 4
Displays the host name before executing the command on the host\&. This option has no effect with the \-p option\&.
.RE
.SH "ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES"
.PP
\fBPRUN_RSH\fR
.RS 4
Specifies a remote shell command\&. The default is
\fBssh\fR\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBPRUN_HOSTFILE\fR
.RS 4
Specifies a hostfile\&. The default is
$HOME/\&.nodelist\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBPRUN_HOSTNAME\fR
.RS 4
Specifies the names of the local host, separated by spaces\&. The default is the output of
\fBhostname\fR
and
\fBhostname \-I\fR\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBPRUN_MAX_JOBS\fR
.RS 4
Specifies the maximum number of parallel jobs\&. The default is 16\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBPRUN_PARALLEL\fR
.RS 4
If it is set to
yes, the command is executed in parallel as with the \-p option\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBPRUN_ALL_INCLUDE_MYSELF\fR
.RS 4
If it is set to
yes, the command is executed also on the local host as with the \-a option\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBPRUN_VERBOSE\fR
.RS 4
If it is set to
yes, the host name is displayed as with the \-v option\&.
.RE
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.PP
\fBgfarm\-prun\fR
exits with 0 when the command succeeds on all hosts\&. Otherwise, it exits with the exit status of the remote shell command for a host on which the command fails\&. When it fails on two or more hosts, the exit status for one of them is returned\&.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.PP
Displays the uptime of all hosts listed in
$HOME/\&.nodelist, except the local host\&.
.sp
.if n \{\
.RS 4
.\}
.nf
	$ gfarm\-prun \-v uptime
.fi
.if n \{\
.RE
.\}
.PP
Restarts gfsd on all hosts listed in
hosts, in parallel\&.
.sp
.if n \{\
.RS 4
.\}
.nf
	$ gfarm\-prun \-p \-h hosts sudo systemctl restart gfsd
.fi
.if n \{\
.RE
.\}
.PP
Executes a local shell script
setup\&.sh
on each host\&.
.sp
.if n \{\
.RS 4
.\}
.nf
	$ gfarm\-prun \-h hosts \-stdin setup\&.sh sh
.fi
.if n \{\
.RE
.\}
.SH "FILES"
.PP
$HOME/\&.nodelist
.RS 4
the default hostfile
.RE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.PP
\fBgfarm-pcp\fR(1),
\fBssh\fR(1)
